# pinned exeuntu source from the retired image workflow is not vendored
exeuntu/
# Bulky third-party payloads inside otherwise-vendored skills: mviz ships sample
# PDFs and screenshots (~1 MB) that no agent needs on a VM. The SKILL.md itself IS
# tracked -- an ignore rule does not affect an already-tracked file -- so the skill
# works; only the ballast is excluded.
#
# herdr used to be excluded the same way, for a full source checkout
# (vendor/libghostty-vt, portable-pty) it no longer ships: upstream is now a single
# 16 KB SKILL.md. The exclusion outlived its reason and quietly broke the skill --
# skills.manifest lists herdr as a `team` row, but nothing under skills/herdr was
# ever committed, so provisioning shipped 36 skills where the manifest asked for 37
# and no VM has ever had it. Removed 2026-08-18.
skills/mviz/*.pdf
skills/mviz/*.png
# generated/local output
*.log

/.quarto/
/.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.quarto_ipynb
/_site/
# provision-docsite's served releases + current symlink (per-VM state, like _site)
/.docsite/
